## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates the ability to design privacy-preserving cross-tenant ML pipelines with real-time inference, deployment discipline, and enterprise-grade governance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-preserving aggregation and differential privacy for cross-tenant insights
- Per-tenant feature stores with isolated data domains
- Vertex AI canary deployments with traffic splitting
- Real-time endpoints with autoscaling and cost budget controls
- Data lineage tracking in Data Catalog
- Drift monitoring (CTR) and latency SLAs logged to BigQuery

## Code Example
```javascript
// Vertex AI Canary Rollout Configuration
const canaryDeployment = {
  endpoint: {
    displayName: 'ad-click-prediction-endpoint',
    model: 'ad-click-model-v1',
    trafficSplit: { '0': 20, '1': 80 } // 20% canary, 80% production
  },
  monitoring: {
    driftThresholds: { ctr: 0.05 },
    latencyThresholds: { p99: 200 },
    alertBudgetPercent: 80
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant inference with strict data residency, budgets, and auditable lineage in a real-world GCP setup.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant isolation in Vertex AI Endpoints and Feature Store namespaces
- Routing logic with per-tenant budget and latency SLAs
- Data Catalog metadata tagging for lineage and governance
- Drift detection and rollback triggers per tenant

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo routing function
async function routeRequest(tenantId, req) {
  const budgetOk = checkBudget(tenantId);
  const latencyOk = checkLatency(tenantId);
  const endpoint = budgetOk && latencyOk ? getTenantEndpoint(tenantId) : getSharedEndpoint();
  return await predict(endpoint, req);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you enforce per-tenant quotas in Feature Store and endpoints?
- How would you simulate rollback scenarios and validate audit trails?
